  body: "# Presumption of occupational cause for prescribed disease\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source
    describes rebuttable presumptions tying particular prescribed diseases to employed-earner employment, with disease-specific
    occupation and timing conditions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 67101 identifies changes from 16 March 2015
    and sends earlier cases to Appendix 6. Not all diseases have the same period or a presumption: C22(b) and B5
    occupation (b) are explicit counterexamples. Presumption is not proof of every benefit condition or a medical
    diagnosis.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 67101, PDF page 19](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=19).\n\
    - [DMG 67102, PDF page 19](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=19).\n\
    - [DMG 67103, PDF page 19](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=19).\n\
    - [DMG 67104, PDF page 20](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=20).\n\
    - [DMG 67105, PDF page 20](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=20).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch67`:
    PDF `3c7414b2ec9ba0ec4073199a063a97072e1bf2c670f1620e241884a39b7e201a`; extracted pages `f6415f436f2f1eea4febaa9f82fbd0ad34a6fc754ce3c59c24fd10311ba0ad12`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.130077Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=19
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/prescribed-disease-occupation
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Each selected presumption is conditioned on a specified disease and occupation; some expressly
      require an onset interval.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch67/0019
      quote: "67102 Where a person has contracted PDs A3(a), A4, A5, A6, A7, A8, A11, B1(a), B3, B4(a), B9, B10,
        B11,\n\nB12, B14, B15, C3, C24A, D4 and D7 there is a presumption1,\n\n\nunless the contrary is proved,
        that the PD is due to the employed earner’s employment if the person who\nhas contracted the PD\n\n\n1.
        was employed in a prescribed occupation2 and\n\n\n2. was so employed on, or at any time within one month
        immediately preceding, the date of onset of the\n\ndisease3.\n\n\nNote 1: There is a different presumption
        for PD A3(b) (see DMG 67103).\n\n\nNote 2: There is a different presumption for PDs B1(b) and B4(b) (see
        DMG 67105).\n\n\n                                       1 SS (II) (PD) Regs, reg 4(1); 2 reg 4(1)(a) & Sch
        1, Part 1; 3 reg 4(1)(b)"
      locator: DMG 67102
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch67/0020
      quote: "67104 Where a person for whom PD B5 is prescribed develops the disease it is presumed, unless the\n\
        contrary is proved, to be due to the nature of their employed earner's employment if\n\n\n1. occupation
        (a) applies and\n\n\n2. the date on which they are treated as having developed the disease is\n\n\n    \
        \  2.1 not less than six weeks after the date on which they were first employed in a prescribed\n      occupation
        (being employed earner's employment) and\n\n\n      2.2 not more than two years after the date on which
        they were last so employed in employed\n\n      earner's employment1.\n\n\nNote 1: See DMG 67481 et seq
        for guidance on PD B5\n\n\nNote 2: There is no presumption for PD B5 occupation (b).\n\n\n             \
        \                                                                      1 SS (II) (PD) Regs, reg 4(3)\n\n\
        \nPrescribed diseases B1(b), B4(b), B7 and B8A"
      locator: DMG 67104
  - target: term/dmg-burden-of-proof
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter states the claimant’s onus while identifying statutory provisions that can operate
      in their favour.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch67/0006
      quote: "67017 The onus of proving that a person is or was suffering from a PD and that the remaining conditions\n\
        for award of benefit under the PD provisions are satisfied rests on the claimant. But there are statutory\n\
        provisions which can operate in the claimant's favour. These relate to\n\n\n1. the satisfaction of the conditions
        for an REA award in pneumoconiosis cases (see DMG Chapter 71)\n\n\n2. the satisfaction of the condition
        that the PD is due to the nature of the employment (see DMG 67101\net seq)\n\n\n3. determining the date
        of onset (see DMG 67249)\n\n\n4. recrudescence (see DMG 67141 et seq)."
      locator: DMG 67017
